+// Two layers: what every xrEndFrame that reaches the runtime must be. A
+// frame with projection layers has exactly two, in the application's order:
+// the periphery layer first with no flags, on the periphery swapchains, then
+// the focus layer with the blend flags, on the focus swapchains; both of one
+// kind (the application's own images, the layer's current copies, or
+// synthetics) and of the same private slot, so both come from one pair; and
+// the focus layer's field of view is the one the application gave the frame
+// whose pose the periphery layer carries. "two:dcs": the focus synthetic's
+// alpha is that frame's.
+void two_layer_check(const XrFrameEndInfo* end_info) {
+    if (end_info == nullptr || end_info->layers == nullptr) {
