+// (b) Head rotation: A's rectangle is not axis-aligned in B. Test (iii)
+// checked the geometry without a rotation only. Here B's head has turned
+// (yaw and pitch, as focus_views; and a roll of 2.9 degrees, which tilts A's
+// edges by up to 6 pixels across the image), and the same is required
+// against A's rectangle carried through both poses: no colour byte differs;
+// no alpha above B's times the cover of the pixel's own direction (2 codes
+// for rounding); alpha 0 more than 1.5 px outside A; B's alpha, every byte,
+// further inside A than the ramp plus kReach (the flow's noise on a still
+// world: 12 px, the GUESS of test iii).
+void test_focus_uncovered_rotation(D3D12WarpFixture& fixture, xrfg::D3D12OpticalFlowBackend backend,
+    const xrfg::D3D12NvidiaOpticalFlowOptions& base) {
